export const synthesis =
  'Chapter 7 turns the existence result of Chapter 6 into the working architecture of practical density-functional calculations. The interacting ground-state density is reproduced by an auxiliary noninteracting system; its orbitals carry the difficult fermionic kinetic structure explicitly through Ts, while Hartree electrostatics is treated classically and all remaining kinetic and interaction differences are assigned to Exc. Variation gives the Kohn–Sham equations, whose effective potential depends on the density and therefore requires a self-consistent fixed point. Variational stationarity explains total-energy, force, and stress formulas, while the behavior of vxc and the derivative discontinuity limits naive interpretations of eigenvalues and gaps. TDDFT and generalized Kohn–Sham theories then show how the auxiliary-system idea can be extended. Chapters 8 and 9 take up the unresolved ingredient that controls practical accuracy: how Exc is approximated.';
